In a general sense, the answer is no I guess. If one is dual-weilding 
Excalibur/Grayswandir and another longsword/silver saber, raw damage caused 
by that combination should be greater than that caused by a joust.
But there are other things to consider, jousting does not trigger passive 
abilities so floating eyes, jellies, molds etc, can be safely dispatched via 
melee combat. It also pushes monsters back a square and seems to stun them 
so than one can act again before them. A lucky streak of jousts probably 
means a monster can be killed without it ever getting a chance to retaliate.

